{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"tracker/tracker.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":158,\\\"end_line\\\":162,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1354,\\\"end_line\\\":1361,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1275,\\\"end_line\\\":1285,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1294,\\\"end_line\\\":1303,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1985,\\\"end_line\\\":2012,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":282,\\\"end_line\\\":287,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":233,\\\"end_line\\\":244,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"node.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":218,\\\"end_line\\\":224,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readme-linearizable\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":27,\\\"end_line\\\":32,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n]\nkn=[\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-singleton-size-only\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"ProgressTracker.IsSingleton returns true exactly when Voters[0] has one member and Voters[1] is empty; it never compares the single voter with the local node id, although its doc comment says the single voting member is the leader.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"tracker.ProgressTracker of any raft instance, including one that is no longer a member of its configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\"]},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-readindex-singleton-answer\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"stepLeader answers MsgReadIndex immediately - with a local ReadState for a local request, or with MsgReadIndexResp for a forwarded one - whenever tracker.IsSingleton() is true, using r.raftLog.committed and without sending any heartbeat or consulting readOnly; otherwise it requires committedEntryInCurrentTerm() and a readOnly round.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"StateLeader; MsgReadIndex; tracker.IsSingleton() true.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\"]},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-removed-leader-keeps-leading\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"When the configuration change that removes the local node is applied while the node is leading, switchToConfig keeps it leading unless Config.StepDownOnRemoval (false by default) is set; the MsgProp path explicitly refuses proposals from a leader that is not in the configuration ('If we are not currently a member of the range ... drop any new proposals') while the MsgReadIndex path has no equivalent guard.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"StateLeader; applyConfChange on a committed change whose resulting configuration does not contain the local node; Config.StepDownOnRemoval false (the default).\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\"]},\n]\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-removed-singleton-leader\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_singleton_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"IsSingleton\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":160,\\\"end_line\\\":160},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"stepLeader\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1275,\\\"end_line\\\":1275},\n ],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe what raft answers for a ReadIndex request that arrives at a node which the application removed from its configuration while it was leading (StepDownOnRemoval false), after the remaining voter has become leader of the reduced single-voter configuration and committed an entry the removed leader never receives.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Two voters {1,2} in one process, ReadOnlySafe, default Config (StepDownOnRemoval false, CheckQuorum false, PreVote false).\\\",\n   \\\"Node 1 is elected leader, then the application proposes and applies the committed configuration change that removes node 1 on both nodes.\\\",\n   \\\"Node 2 campaigns and commits one entry; no message from the current configuration reaches node 1 (its heartbeats at the old term are ignored by node 2 because CheckQuorum and PreVote are disabled).\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Lease-based reads (ReadOnlyLeaseBased).\\\",\\\"Check-quorum and pre-vote configurations, which give a leader another way to learn that it is stale.\\\",\\\"Snapshot transfer and asynchronous storage writes.\\\"]},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Elect node 1 leader of {1,2} with a real MsgHup/MsgVote round, let the application apply the committed empty entry, propose and apply the removal of node 1 on both nodes, then elect node 2 in the reduced configuration {2} and commit one proposal on it; then issue MsgReadIndex to node 1, then the same request to node 2, then three heartbeat intervals on node 1 and a second MsgReadIndex to node 1.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A ReadIndex answer must let the application serve a linearizable read (raft.go:233-244 and README.md:27-32 state that ReadOnlySafe achieves linearizability by communicating with the quorum, and node.go:218-224 states that once the application advances past the returned read index, linearizable reads issued before the request can be processed safely). The tracker's own comment for IsSingleton says the single voting member is the leader, so answering locally without any check is only sound when that member is the local node.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"raft (target): the singleton shortcut in the ReadIndex path decides the answer for the whole configuration, and the library already refuses proposals from a leader that is not in its own configuration.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"setup\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\"},\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"state\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"StateLeader\\\"},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The node whose removal the application applied is still leading, with a configuration whose single voter is another node (singleton true, is_voter false).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"actual_leader_ahead\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The actual leader of the reduced configuration has committed an entry that the removed leader's commit index does not cover (committed 4 vs 2).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_other_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_states\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Witness: the removed leader answered the ReadIndex request with index 2, below the commit index 4 the actual leader already had, without sending any message (heartbeats_emitted 0, messages_emitted empty, pending_reads 0).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_own_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same request answered by the node that is the actual leader of the configuration returns an index that covers its commit index, so the local singleton answer is only unsafe on the node that is no longer the voter.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"second_stale_read\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"same_stale_index_as_first\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"No repair from the periodic path: after three heartbeat intervals and no replies from the current configuration, the removed leader is still leading at its old term and still answers with the same stale index.\\\"},\n ],\n}\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Opened a safety-oriented investigation after the first question's account was recorded: the ReadIndex singleton shortcut is taken from tracker.IsSingleton, which only checks the size of the configuration, and the MsgReadIndex path answers locally on that basis while the analogous write path refuses proposals from a leader that is not in its configuration. Sources, behaviors and the required anchors are recorded and one formal execution of the two-node probe assurance_singleton_test.go is requested.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":src,\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@readindex-removed-singleton-leader\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does raft answer a ReadIndex request on a node that is no longer a voter of its own configuration when that configuration has exactly one voter, and can such an answer be stale relative to what the actual leader of that configuration has already committed?\\\",\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"tracker.IsSingleton() only checks that the configuration has one voter, and stepLeader answers MsgReadIndex locally whenever it is true. A leader whose removal the application applied (StepDownOnRemoval false) therefore keeps answering reads immediately with its own, frozen commit index, even though the library knows from its own tracker that the single voter is another node; the write path guards exactly this case, the read path does not.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\"],\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether a node in StateLeader whose configuration contains exactly one other voter answers MsgReadIndex with no outgoing heartbeat and no readOnly activity, and whether the returned index is below the commit index of the node that is the actual leader of that configuration.\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":kn,\n \\\"gaps\\\":[{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-removed-singleton-leader\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Which permitted sequence establishes a singleton configuration that excludes the local leader without stepping it down, and which node then holds the current commit index?\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-removed-singleton-leader\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\",\\\"readme-linearizable\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The source account: tracker.IsSingleton (tracker/tracker.go:158-162) is a size test - one member in Voters[0] and none in Voters[1] - and its doc comment asserts that this member is the leader, but nothing compares it with the local node id. stepLeader's MsgReadIndex case (raft.go:1354-1361) takes that test as sufficient authority to answer immediately from r.raftLog.committed, for a local request by appending a ReadState and for a forwarded request by sending MsgReadIndexResp, without any heartbeat or readOnly round. The library reaches this state legitimately: applying a committed configuration change that removes the local node while it is leading leaves it leading unless Config.StepDownOnRemoval is set (raft.go:1985-2012 with the documented default false at raft.go:282-287), and its tracker then holds a configuration whose only voter is another node. The same library refuses new proposals from exactly this node (raft.go:1294-1303: 'If we are not currently a member of the range (i.e. this node was removed from the configuration while serving as leader), drop any new proposals'), so the responsibility for the removed leader's behaviour is taken up on the write path and left open on the read path. The consequence is a safety claim, not a progress claim: ReadOnlySafe is documented as achieving linearizability by communicating with the quorum (raft.go:233-244) and ReadIndex promises that work issued before the request can be served once the application has advanced past the returned index (node.go:218-224, README.md:27-32). A client that issues its read through the removed leader - a node that still reports itself as the leader - is handed an index that is below entries already committed by the actual leader of that configuration, so the state it is licensed to serve may miss a write that completed before the read began, and retrying at the same node reproduces the same answer instead of repairing it. The draft probe exercises both halves: it observes the removed leader (config voters=(2), singleton true, is_voter false, still StateLeader) answering MsgReadIndex with read index 2 while the actual leader had already committed index 4, emitting no message at all, and it observes the same request answered by the actual leader with an index that covers its commit index; three later heartbeat intervals produce no reply and the removed leader repeats the same stale index. The formal execution of this harness is requested with this update, so this remains a source-grounded account until its receipt exists.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"A client is expected to direct linearizable reads at the current leader; reading through a node that was removed is a client-side premise. The library cannot detect staleness in general: a leader that was removed by a configuration change it has already applied, or one partitioned away, also answers old-term requests until it hears a higher term.\\\",\n   \\\"What makes this case the library's responsibility rather than the client's is narrower: the shortcut is taken from the local tracker, which already establishes that the only voter is another node, and the library refuses proposals from that same node; without the shortcut the read would need a quorum acknowledgement from the current configuration, and the removed leader cannot obtain one once the actual leader has moved to a higher term (its heartbeat is ignored or answered with a higher term).\\\",\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The scenario requires the application to apply a committed configuration change that removes the leading node while Config.StepDownOnRemoval is false; applications that set that option, or that stop the removed node, do not reach it.\\\",\n   \\\"The removed leader remains at its old term only while nothing from the current configuration carries a higher term to it; with CheckQuorum or PreVote enabled the current leader answers the stale heartbeat with its higher term and the removed leader steps down, which bounds the window but does not remove the stale answers issued before that.\\\",\n   \\\"Only the declared probe has been run natively so far; the retained receipt for this harness is still outstanding, and no bound is claimed for how long a client that never retries elsewhere stays exposed.\\\"]}]}\nu[\\\"experiment\\\"]=exp\nopen('update3.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update3.json 2>&1 | tail -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"tracker/tracker.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":158,\\\"end_line\\\":162,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1354,\\\"end_line\\\":1361,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1275,\\\"end_line\\\":1285,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1294,\\\"end_line\\\":1303,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1985,\\\"end_line\\\":2012,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":282,\\\"end_line\\\":287,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":233,\\\"end_line\\\":244,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"node.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":218,\\\"end_line\\\":224,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"readme-linearizable\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":27,\\\"end_line\\\":32,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n]\nkn=[\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-singleton-size-only\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"ProgressTracker.IsSingleton returns true exactly when Voters[0] has one member and Voters[1] is empty; it never compares the single voter with the local node id, although its doc comment says the single voting member is the leader.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"tracker.ProgressTracker of any raft instance, including one that is no longer a member of its configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\"]},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-readindex-singleton-answer\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"stepLeader answers MsgReadIndex immediately - with a local ReadState for a local request, or with MsgReadIndexResp for a forwarded one - whenever tracker.IsSingleton() is true, using r.raftLog.committed and without sending any heartbeat or consulting readOnly; otherwise it requires committedEntryInCurrentTerm() and a readOnly round.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"StateLeader; MsgReadIndex; tracker.IsSingleton() true.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\"]},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-removed-leader-keeps-leading\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"When the configuration change that removes the local node is applied while the node is leading, switchToConfig keeps it leading unless Config.StepDownOnRemoval (false by default) is set; the MsgProp path explicitly refuses proposals from a leader that is not in the configuration ('If we are not currently a member of the range ... drop any new proposals') while the MsgReadIndex path has no equivalent guard.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"StateLeader; applyConfChange on a committed change whose resulting configuration does not contain the local node; Config.StepDownOnRemoval false (the default).\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\"]},\n]\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-removed-singleton-leader\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_singleton_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"IsSingleton\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":160,\\\"end_line\\\":160},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"stepLeader\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1275,\\\"end_line\\\":1275},\n ],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe what raft answers for a ReadIndex request that arrives at a node which the application removed from its configuration while it was leading (StepDownOnRemoval false), after the remaining voter has become leader of the reduced single-voter configuration and committed an entry the removed leader never receives.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Two voters {1,2} in one process, ReadOnlySafe, default Config (StepDownOnRemoval false, CheckQuorum false, PreVote false).\\\",\n   \\\"Node 1 is elected leader, then the application proposes and applies the committed configuration change that removes node 1 on both nodes.\\\",\n   \\\"Node 2 campaigns and commits one entry; no message from the current configuration reaches node 1 (its heartbeats at the old term are ignored by node 2 because CheckQuorum and PreVote are disabled).\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Lease-based reads (ReadOnlyLeaseBased).\\\",\\\"Check-quorum and pre-vote configurations, which give a leader another way to learn that it is stale.\\\",\\\"Snapshot transfer and asynchronous storage writes.\\\"]},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Elect node 1 leader of {1,2} with a real MsgHup/MsgVote round, let the application apply the committed empty entry, propose and apply the removal of node 1 on both nodes, then elect node 2 in the reduced configuration {2} and commit one proposal on it; then issue MsgReadIndex to node 1, then the same request to node 2, then three heartbeat intervals on node 1 and a second MsgReadIndex to node 1.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A ReadIndex answer must let the application serve a linearizable read (raft.go:233-244 and README.md:27-32 state that ReadOnlySafe achieves linearizability by communicating with the quorum, and node.go:218-224 states that once the application advances past the returned read index, linearizable reads issued before the request can be processed safely). The tracker's own comment for IsSingleton says the single voting member is the leader, so answering locally without any check is only sound when that member is the local node.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"raft (target): the singleton shortcut in the ReadIndex path decides the answer for the whole configuration, and the library already refuses proposals from a leader that is not in its own configuration.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"setup\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\"},\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"state\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"StateLeader\\\"},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The node whose removal the application applied is still leading, with a configuration whose single voter is another node (singleton true, is_voter false).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"actual_leader_ahead\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The actual leader of the reduced configuration has committed an entry that the removed leader's commit index does not cover (committed 4 vs 2).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_other_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_states\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Witness: the removed leader answered the ReadIndex request with index 2, below the commit index 4 the actual leader already had, without sending any message (heartbeats_emitted 0, messages_emitted empty, pending_reads 0).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_own_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same request answered by the node that is the actual leader of the configuration returns an index that covers its commit index, so the local singleton answer is only unsafe on the node that is no longer the voter.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"second_stale_read\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"step\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"same_stale_index_as_first\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"No repair from the periodic path: after three heartbeat intervals and no replies from the current configuration, the removed leader is still leading at its old term and still answers with the same stale index.\\\"},\n ],\n}\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Opened a safety-oriented investigation after the first question's account was recorded: the ReadIndex singleton shortcut is taken from tracker.IsSingleton, which only checks the size of the configuration, and the MsgReadIndex path answers locally on that basis while the analogous write path refuses proposals from a leader that is not in its configuration. Sources, behaviors and the required anchors are recorded a